   296	one fixed-degree Hilbert-function value does not determine dimension (in `P^2` at the stable
   297	`N = 2`, a line and three noncollinear reduced points both have `HF = 3` but dimensions 1 and 0 --
   298	verdict O6). **P2 (distance):** needs a closest-pair nondegeneracy (Morse-Bott) promise. **P3
   299	(integration):** needs encoding, degree, norm and projective bihomogeneity promises for `g`.
   300	Only P0 is fully specified.
   301	
   302	**2 -- Classical baseline: NOT MET.** r0's K-IO2 squeeze is retracted (O6). What can honestly be
   303	said: (i) `I_N + J_N` is the row span of the concatenated degree-`N` Macaulay matrices
   304	(D-macaulay-matrix), so no elimination is avoided by the quantum route; (ii) numerical irreducible
   305	decomposition [SVW, DOI 10.1137/S0036142900372549], the diagonal homotopy [SVW,
   306	DOI 10.1137/S0036142903430463] and the trace test [SVW, DOI 10.1137/S0036142901397101] are the
   307	relevant competitors **once witness sets for `V` and `W` are already supplied and the tracking is
   308	well conditioned**; the cited papers do not establish a universal `deg V . deg W` path bound, exact
   309	certification, or polynomial cost from sparse generators, and Lairez [DOI 10.1007/s10208-016-9319-7,
   310	arXiv:1507.05485] proves average-case polynomial time for one approximate root in a specific model,
   311	not per-path polynomial cost for every diagonal homotopy here. (iii) For P0 the comparator is
   312	Hutch++ [arXiv:2010.09649]; see criterion 4. No adjudicated best classical algorithm for P1 is
   313	established by this lane.
   314	
   315	**3 -- Quantum algorithm: NOT MET.** Write `gamma_N = Delta_N/alpha_BE` (D-normalised-gap,
   316	D-block-encoding-normalisation). A spectral filter `P_I` costs `O~(gamma_N^{-1} log(1/eps'))`
   317	block-encoding uses (D-qsvt). The registered D-dqc1-style-estimate is
   318	`O(eps^{-2})` repetitions on the maximally mixed valid-sector state, so estimating `tau_N` to
   319	additive `eps` costs `O~(gamma_N^{-1} eps^{-2})` queries, times `poly(n, log N)` per query.
   320	`O(eps^{-1})` requires a coherent purification/preparation and BQP-style amplitude estimation, which
   321	is **not** the registered DQC1 procedure (verdict O5). Space `O(n log N)` qubits versus `M_N` words
   322	is not by itself a separation (fact SP-0, PRD D15). There is no proved family with a complete
   323	resource bound beating the best baseline, so this criterion is not met.
   324	
   325	**4 -- Dequantization audit: NOT MET (redone at r1).** Low-rank dequantization does not apply
   326	(`H_N` sparse and high rank, `rank P_I = HF(N)`; D-hardness-anchors). Single error model, as the
   327	critic demands: `A = P_I P_J P_I >= 0`, `tau_N = Tr(A)/M_N`. **Classical:** Hutch++ gives relative
   328	error `delta` in `O(1/delta)` applications of `A`; each application needs **three** projector
   329	filters, each `O~(M_N s_row gamma_N^{-1})` flops by sparse Krylov. For additive `eps` in `tau_N`,
   330	`delta = eps/tau_N`, i.e. `O(tau_N/eps)` applications, so
   331	`O~(M_N s_row gamma_N^{-1} tau_N/eps)` flops. **Quantum (registered DQC1):**
   332	`O~(gamma_N^{-1} eps^{-2})` queries. Ratio classical/quantum `= M_N s_row tau_N eps`. So the only
   333	margin is the vector length `M_N` (times `s_row tau_N eps`), and it **shrinks as `eps` shrinks**,
   334	because Hutch++ is `1/eps` where registered DQC1 sampling is `1/eps^2`; with BQP amplitude
   335	estimation the ratio becomes `M_N s_row tau_N`, a clean vector-length margin. The margin is arm A's
