   413	## Proposed definitions
   414	
   415	MERGE PROPOSAL (`definitions/definitions.md`). Texts below are the r1 critic's adjudicated
   416	rewordings, verbatim, with the verdict's inline LaTeX rendered in this memo's ASCII convention.
   417	
   418	**D-intersection-overlap (ACCEPT).** `T_N(I,J) := Tr(P_{0,N}^{(I)}P_{0,N}^{(J)})`, `P_{0,N}` the
   419	projector onto `ker H_N` (D-projectors), i.e. the Bergman projector of D-bergman-projector;
   420	equivalently `||B_I^dag B_J||_F^2` for orthonormal ground-space bases, and `= Tr(P_I P_J P_I) >= 0`.
   421	Three normalisations, all in use: `tau_N = T_N/M_N` (the D-dqc1-style-estimate quantity),
   422	`T_N/sqrt(HF_I HF_J)`, `T_N/(HF_I HF_J) = Tr(rho_I rho_J)` (what a two-copy SWAP test measures).
   423	Pitfalls: it is **not** `Tr(P_{I_N}P_{J_N}) = M_N - HF_I - HF_J + T_N = Theta(M_N)`; the seed's
   424	Conjecture 8.10(a) and rows C-085, C-166, C-167 do not say which projector they mean, and only this
   425	reading has the asserted geometric asymptotics -- those rows should be amended to cite this id
   426	(folded in here from the rejected C-NEW-IO-PROJECTOR-AMBIGUITY row). The three normalisations differ
   427	by factors exponential in codimension, so a signal-size statement must say which.
   428	
   429	**D-clean-intersection (REWORD, verbatim).** "Smooth `V, W` in `CP^n` intersect cleanly along a
   430	smooth pure-dimensional `Z = V ^ W` if `T_xZ = T_xV ^ T_xW` for every `x in Z`. Transverse
   431	intersections are clean; clean intersections may have excess dimension."
   432	
   433	**D-intersection-angle-condition-number (REWORD, verbatim).** "For a clean intersection, let
   434	`A_x = T_xV (-) T_xZ` and `B_x = T_xW (-) T_xZ`. Define `J(x) = prod_i sin^2 theta_i(x)`, padding the
   435	principal-angle list with `pi/2` when the dimensions differ, and `mu_cap = sup_Z J^{-1} < infinity`.
   436	No universal crossover scale follows from this definition alone."
   437	
   438	**D-bergman-frame-operator (REWORD, verbatim).** "Define
   439	`S_V^{(N)} = int_V |e_p><e_p| dvol_V(p)`. Exactly, `ran S_V^{(N)} = (I(V)_N)^perp`. The claimed
   440	operator-norm asymptotic `S_V^{(N)} = (pi/N)^k(P_{I(V),N} + O(N^{-1}))` is a separate
   441	conjectural/theorem claim requiring a precise source; it is not part of the definition."
   442	
   443	**D-normalised-toeplitz-operator (REWORD, verbatim).** "For `N >= r` and a projective bihomogeneous
   444	symbol `g(z, conj z)` of bidegree `(r,r)`, define
   445	`T~_g^{(N)} = ((N-r)!/N!) P_{0,N} :g(a^dag,a): P_{0,N}`. If `I` is radical, `N` is stable and
   446	`p in V(I)`, its restricted coherent-state symbol is exactly `g(p, conj p)`." (Not an amendment to
   447	D-toeplitz-operator: a distinct definition, per verdict O3.)
   448	
   449	**D-contact-order (REWORD, verbatim).** "At a common point of smooth plane curves choose holomorphic
   450	coordinates unitary for the Fubini-Study metric at the point and flatten `W` to `v = 0`. If `V` has
   451	`v = gamma u^m + O(u^{m+1})`, `gamma != 0`, then `m` is the contact order and local intersection
   452	multiplicity. `m = 1` is transverse; `m >= 2` is tangent."
   453	
