J. EXACT identity for linear V, W (new in repair r1; it is the
   opening identity of verdict O1, proved here and tested).
   For subspaces U, W of C^{n+1} with principal cosines
   sigma_1..sigma_r, r = min(dim U, dim W):
     Tr(P_{Sym^N U} P_{Sym^N W}) = h_N(sigma_1^2, ..., sigma_r^2),
   h_N the complete homogeneous symmetric polynomial.  Proof: in
   principal-vector bases <u_i, w_j> = sigma_i delta_ij, so the
   symmetrised monomial bases have overlap prod_i sigma_i^{alpha_i}
   diagonally in the multi-index alpha, |alpha| = N.
   Every linear table in this script is a special case:
     two lines in P^2         sigma = (1, c)       -> sum_a c^{2a}
     two planes in P^3        sigma = (1, 1, c)    -> sum_a c^{2a}(N+1-a)
     Clifford skew pair       sigma = (c, c)       -> (N+1)c^{2N}
     excess planes in P^4     sigma = (1, 1, 0)    -> N+1
     hyperplanes in P^n       sigma = (1^{n-1}, c) -> sum_a c^{2a}C(N-a+n-2,n-2)

   random subspaces in C^4, C^5, C^6, N = 4..7: worst relative discrepancy 2.300e-15
   => the whole linear half of arm C is EXACT, needs no Bergman
      frame lemma, and needs no Laplace argument.

